### Phase 2 — Auth + JWT through the Gateway

### Auth health via Gateway (no JWT)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/health

### JWKS public keys (Gateway may call Auth directly on 8081)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/auth/.well-known/jwks.json

### Register (always becomes CUSTOMER — clients cannot self-assign ADMIN)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "learner@stayfinder.local",
  "password": "Password@123"
}

### Login as seeded customer
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@stayfinder.local",
  "password": "Customer@123"
}

### Login as seeded admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@stayfinder.local",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

### Current user (replace TOKEN)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN

### Customer token against admin endpoint — expect 403
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/admin-check
Authorization: Bearer CUSTOMER_TOKEN

### Admin token against admin endpoint — expect 200
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/admin-check
Authorization: Bearer ADMIN_TOKEN

### Missing JWT against /me — expect 401
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me

### Public catalog path, booking-service not running — expect 503 even without JWT
GET http://localhost:8080/api/bookings/hotels

### Protected booking write, booking-service not running — expect 503 with a valid JWT
POST http://localhost:8080/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer TOKEN
Content-Type: application/json

{}
